---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../component-docs/CodeBlock.astro';
import TokenTable from './TokenTable.astro';
import {registry,pending,coverage,tokenPages,type TokenTopic} from '../../tokens/registry';
import {href} from '../../data';
import '../../styles/component-docs.css';
import '../../styles/token-docs.css';
const {topic}=Astro.props as {topic:TokenTopic};
const filter=(t:typeof registry[number])=>topic.slug==='primitives'?t.tier==='Primitives':topic.slug==='semantic'?t.tier!=='Primitives':topic.slug==='colour'?t.name.startsWith('color/')||t.type==='color':topic.slug==='typography'?t.id.includes('/type/')||t.id.includes('/font/'):topic.slug==='spacing'?t.id.includes('/space/'):topic.slug==='radius'?t.id.includes('/radius/'):topic.slug==='elevation'?t.type==='shadow':topic.slug==='responsive'?t.id.includes('/layout/'):true;
const rows=registry.filter(filter);
const examples:Record<string,string>={
 '':`Primitives/color/mulberry/600 → Semantic/color/action/primary/default\n→ Component/button/color/action/primary/default\n\nLight: #742653\nDark semantic alias: Primitives/color/mulberry/200 (#EFBFD9)`,
 primitives:JSON.stringify({'color/mulberry/600':{$type:'color',$value:'#742653',$extensions:{samvad:{status:'foundation-approved'}}}},null,2),
 semantic:JSON.stringify({'color/action/primary/default':{$type:'color',$value:{Light:'{Primitives/color/mulberry/600}',Dark:'{Primitives/color/mulberry/200}'},$extensions:{samvad:{status:'implementation-candidate'}}}},null,2),
 colour:'.example-action {\n  background: var(--samvad-component-button-color-action-primary-default);\n  color: var(--samvad-component-button-color-action-on-solid);\n}\n/* Existing Button consumes these aliases. No direct primitive use. */',
 typography:'.example-label {\n  font-family: var(--samvad-semantic-font-family-primary);\n  font-size: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-size);\n  line-height: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-line-height);\n  font-weight: var(--samvad-semantic-type-label-weight);\n}',
 spacing:'.example-layout {\n  gap: var(--samvad-semantic-space-scale-16);\n  padding: var(--samvad-semantic-space-scale-24);\n}',
 radius:'.example-surface {\n  border-radius: var(--samvad-semantic-radius-md);\n}',
 elevation:'.example-surface {\n  box-shadow: var(--samvad-semantic-elevation-2);\n}\n/* A foundation shadow example; not a retroactive field-shadow decision. */',
 responsive:'/* CSS custom properties cannot drive native media-query conditions. */\n@media (min-width: 600px) {\n  .example-layout { gap: var(--samvad-semantic-layout-gutter-medium); }\n}\n/* Literal breakpoint is validated against the source. See responsive.json. */',
 'css-variables':'/* From website/src/styles/ (the existing project): */\n@import "../../../design-system/tokens/dist/tokens.css";\n\n.example { color: var(--samvad-semantic-color-text-primary); }\n/* Switch an ancestor data-theme="light" / data-theme="dark". */'
};
const toc=[{id:'contract',label:'Scope and contract'},{id:'values',label:'Token table'},{id:'implementation',label:'Usage and exports'},{id:'mapping',label:'Component mapping'},{id:'pending',label:'Pending decisions'}];
---
<DocsLayout page={topic.id} toc={toc}>
 <article class="component-docs token-docs">
 <section id="contract" class="doc-section"><h2>Traceable values. Explicit decisions.</h2>
 <p class="component-preview-notice"><strong>Implemented locally · not a ratified public package.</strong> Raw values come from approved foundations and explicitly approved component exceptions. Semantic and component role assignments preserve existing implementations and are tagged <code>implementation-candidate</code> where production ratification was previously pending. The five reviewed decisions are tagged <code>decision-approved</code>; this does not ratify unrelated candidate roles. Website-only <code>--docs-*</code> adapters remain separate.</p>
 <p>{registry.filter(t=>t.tier==='Primitives').length} primitives → {registry.filter(t=>t.tier==='Semantic').length} semantic aliases → {registry.filter(t=>t.tier==='Component').length} component aliases. The sources use predictable slash names and a local JSON contract with <code>$type</code>, <code>$value</code>, explicit Light/Dark values and provenance. This is not a claim of conformance to an external interchange standard or a native Figma variable library.</p>
 <p>{topic.slug==='typography'?'Sizes and line heights are serialized to rem against the approved 16px reference without locking the user’s root size. Geist/Geist Mono source names are adapted to the existing installed variable-font family names. Field/selection labels now use approved label 14/20/600; helper/error copy uses body/s 14/22/400. OTP tracking is an approved functional exception. Weight 500 in Badge/Table and other unitless line-height assignments remain deferred.':topic.slug==='elevation'?'All five approved foundation levels are exported in both modes. Popover now uses elevation/2. Fields retain their approved soft-shadow exception, including existing Dark pigment. Toast retains its geometry and alpha with neutral/950 pigment in both modes; its Dark alpha remains a documented exception to elevation/4.':topic.slug==='responsive'?'Approved breakpoints are 600px and 1024px; compact/medium/wide gutters and margins are exported. Content maxima are 640, 960 and 1200; reading starts at 65ch. Responsive CSS exports use literal media queries generated from the source. Component 1/2/3 column defaults do not replace the approved 4/8/12 page grid.':topic.slug==='spacing'?'The complete approved spacing scale is exported. Components use component aliases or semantic scale aliases for supported values. The neutral scale aliases intentionally encode a utility scale; their placement in specific roles remains candidate metadata.':topic.slug==='radius'?'none, xs, sm, md, lg, xl and full are exported. Equivalent 999px capsules/circles now consume approved full=9999 through a shared component alias. Functional geometry outside that reviewed mapping remains explicit.':'Aliases are validated for existing references, matching types, tier direction and cycles. Components do not consume primitive CSS variables directly. Light/Dark switching uses data-theme; nested theme scopes redeclare alias chains to prevent inherited light-mode values leaking into dark previews.'}</p>
 <div class="token-page-links">{tokenPages.filter(p=>p.id!==topic.id).map(p=><a href={href(`design-tokens/${p.slug?p.slug+'/':''}`)}>{p.title}</a>)}</div>
 </section>
 <section id="values" class="doc-section"><h2>{topic.slug==='semantic'?'Semantic and component aliases':'Token source table'}</h2><p>Both resolved mode values, status and source are shown. Responsive overrides are recorded in the JSON exports; this table’s Light/Dark columns show compact/base values. Search does not change any design value.</p><TokenTable id={topic.id} rows={rows}/></section>
 <section id="implementation" class="doc-section"><h2>Usage and exports</h2><CodeBlock code={examples[topic.slug]} language={['','primitives','semantic'].includes(topic.slug)?(topic.slug?'JSON':'Text'):'CSS'}/>
 <p>Source files: <code>design-system/tokens/source/</code>. Run <code>npm run tokens:build</code> from <code>website/</code> to regenerate CSS, resolved data, typed CSS names and documentation downloads. <code>npm run tokens:check</code> detects stale exports. Edit sources, never generated files. The website build runs the token generator automatically.</p>
 <ul>{['tokens.css','primitives.json','semantic.json','components.json','registry.json','resolved.json','css-variables.ts','responsive.json','pending.json','component-coverage.json'].map(file=><li><a href={href('tokens/'+file)} download>{file}</a></li>)}</ul>
 <p>Use Component aliases for existing component roles and Semantic aliases for shared styles. Primitive exports are for architecture/debugging and future adapters. Do not depend on website-only <code>--docs-*</code> or private <code>--_*</code> implementation variables as a production API. Fonts must still be loaded by the consuming application.</p>
 </section>
 <section id="mapping" class="doc-section"><h2>49 families. Supported connections, honest limits.</h2><p>All 49 families were inventoried before mapping. Their shared Actions, Field/ChoiceGroup, Library and Layout implementations now consume the supported token aliases. This is a partial property migration, not a claim that every literal has been tokenized. Existing runtime choices, native control attributes and unsupported values remain explicit.</p>
 <details><summary>Inspect all component mappings</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Family</th><th scope="col">Shared style source</th><th scope="col">Mapping status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{coverage.map(c=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={href(`components/${c.group}/${c.slug}/`)}>{c.slug}</a></th><td><code>{c.styleSource}</code></td><td>{c.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
 </section>
 <section id="pending" class="doc-section"><h2>Pending decisions remain visible.</h2><p>{pending.items.length} retained CSS declarations are recorded with selectors and reasons. The list includes unsupported design assignments and functional geometry, so it is not a count of independent design decisions. Approved field/toast shadows, 56px large controls and loading cadence are explicitly tokenized exceptions. OTP tracking remains an approved functional declaration. Deferred entries are not implied to be approved.</p>
 <p>Remaining decisions: unrelated candidate role names/assignments; Badge/Table weight 500; non-equivalent line-height roles; unreviewed functional/decorative geometry and composite indicators/borders; standalone packaging and platform adapters. Approved quiet Dark borders now use neutral/800, focus offsets use 2px, ordinary button easing is standard, and loading cadence remains 960ms with reduced-motion support. Source font fallbacks do not imply that Noto fonts have been bundled.</p>
 <details><summary>Inspect retained declarations</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source / selector</th><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Retained value / reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pending.items.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><small>{p.file}</small><br/><code>{p.selector}</code></th><td>{p.property}</td><td><code>{p.value}</code><br/><small>{p.reason}</small></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
 <p>Figma was not modified. This phase does not create Figma collections, change the single-page constraint, publish a package, or begin Patterns or Resources.</p>
 </section>
 </article>
</DocsLayout>
